RKE2-Install ist amd64-hardcoded (share/Rexfile:487-500): rke2.linux-amd64.tar.gz + sha256sum-amd64.txt fest verdrahtet, laeuft auf aarch64 in 404.

Gefunden beim Test gegen cortex.ai.citilan.de (NVIDIA DGX Spark, GB10, aarch64, Ubuntu 24.04).

Cilium-Tasks (Rexfile:864, :998) machen arch-Detection bereits korrekt — das Muster ist da, RKE2 nutzt es nicht.

Auch verdaechtig: linux-headers-amd64 in der NVIDIA-Driver-Paketliste (Rexfile:288, Debian-Zweig).

Ziel: jede Binary-Download-URL, jede Paketliste und jedes Container-Image im Repo arch-aware oder nachweislich multi-arch. Nicht nur RKE2 flicken — vollstaendiger Audit.
Audit done, fix landed in the working tree (share/Rexfile, Dockerfile, t/35-multi-arch.t). make test green: 35 files, 647 tests.

Fixed:
- share/Rexfile: new _node_arch() helper (uname -m -> GOARCH, unmapped machines pass through so the failing URL names them). install_rke2_server now builds rke2.linux-$arch.tar.gz + sha256sum-$arch.txt, downloads to those names and size-checks the file it actually wrote; verified against get.rke2.io, which looks for exactly ${ARTIFACT_PATH}/rke2.${SUFFIX}.tar.gz and sha256sum-${ARCH}.txt. Confirmed rancher/rke2 publishes both arm64 assets.
- share/Rexfile: the two inlined Cilium ternary chains now call the helper (pattern exists once, not four times).
- share/Rexfile install_nvidia: linux-headers-amd64 -> dpkg --print-architecture; and the whole driver install is now skipped when _nvidia_driver_present() (nvidia-smi enumerates GPUs AND libcuda.so present). That is the DGX Spark protection — before this, Ubuntu hosts got nvidia-driver-535 pulled over the vendor driver.
- Dockerfile: kubectl download used bin/linux/amd64; now dpkg --print-architecture.

Verified clean, no change needed: k3s (install script self-detects, OCP passes only VERSION/TOKEN/NODE_NAME/URL), rke2 agent (piped install script, self-detects), NVIDIA container-toolkit apt source (uses aptbs own $(ARCH) substitution; arm64 dir exists upstream), registries.yaml + containerd nvidia config + RKE2/k3s config generation (arch-neutral), no arch nodeSelectors anywhere, OCP::Versions holds no arch-bound artifact names.

Container images: all third-party pins verified multi-arch with a real linux/arm64 entry under the same tag (NFD, gpu-operator, container-toolkit, k8s-device-plugin, dcgm-exporter, dcgm, cilium, operator-generic, registry:2, cert-manager, debian:trixie, perl:5.40-slim). No sbsa/aarch64 tag switching needed.

Split off: #10 (CI publishes amd64-only — the robocop blocker), #11 (gpu-operator-validator v26.3.3 does not exist at all), #12 (no arm64 path for a bare NVIDIA driver install), #13 (gpu_enabled/gpu_driver dead config), #14 (Hetzner x86 filter, latent).
